we see that main allocates a buffer of 64 bytes and 4 bytes for pointer to the function, then it asigns the pointer to the function and then it calls strcpy that copies the argument to the buffer and then it calls the function pointer.

we check the code segment of the program to see if there's anthing interesting and we found two functions the first one is the function m()
